employs an initializer list that prefaces the constructor’s definition with a colon and a call
to a base class A constructor. We discussed initializer lists in Section 3.8.3 in the context of
const class members. In the inheritance setting initializer lists serve the purpose of forcing
the creation of the members of the inherited base class object prior to the construction of
any that are unique to the derived class. This is essentially the only way derived objects
can be initialized.
